{"ts":"2026-09-05T17:54:56.734Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"grok-4.6","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"7aef5f1edda5a7a8739a0176","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"grok-4.6","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-05T17:54:56.734Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-09-05T17:54:56.734Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Pinned exact devDependencies: @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.9.5, pm-changelog 2026.9.2, pm-ops 2026.9.5. npm run release:check exited 0. ./node_modules/.bin/pm health --strict-exit exited 0.\n\nThe date gate already asserted the unflagged heading differs from the flagged one. Live generator output after the pin:\n  with --date-from-version: ## 2026.1.2 - 2026-01-02\n  without: ## 2026.1.2\n\nRevert-proof of that property against this generator: temporarily requiring the clock-derived heading failed 4 of 24 tests in test/verify-release-changelog-date.test.ts (exit 1). Restoring the difference assertion passed 24 of 24 (exit 0). Failures were:\n  a control identical to the flagged run fails, because then the flag discriminates nothing\n  a control derived some other way still passes, because the contract is that the flag changes the heading\n  verify runs both halves against this checkout and reports through the process streams\n  main verifies this checkout and reports through the process streams\n\nNo verifier source change was needed; those tests were already on main."}]}],"before_hash":"dcea672a051bb07b1cf41d1e5c36b60c6d69a896f9758432bc14c46f4ea165bd","after_hash":"e08998c89c1d87e0c5ebfb0366faa8c698f322ec32fe27c9563f92d84e9d46a1","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"890b637a890fc1ef42faf456eb8dc5aa5bd40f62fd4db9eacaf7d08bada81b0d"}
